# rm384, the smoked-glass rehearsal (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm384
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_edda_gullford
written_by codex
title the smoked-glass rehearsal
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk rehearses_a_verse_in_the_dark_patch_on_a_lamp_glass
likes honey_cakes singing quiet_chapel summer_evenings
dislikes crowds flies
fears a_wick_burning_unseen a_voice_among_strange_elbows
hopes a_pitch_with_one_stool a_song_sung_after_the_shutters_close
topics pastimes +0.4 work +0.4 faith +0.3 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=quiet gossip=withheld refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# rehearses songs to the dark patches in a lamp glass, looks for a clear path before stepping into a crowd, and keeps the quiet verses for familiar ears.

words
oath! = Tallow and tidewash | Smoke in my teeth
saying! = Let the soot hear the rehearsal | One lamp for the walk, one song for myself
sootmask = a dark crescent on the glass | a smudge like a listening ear
songcloth = my folded lamp rag | a blackened square
glasseye = the little clear patch | a bare oval of glass
stallpot = my metal savings pot | a pot with a narrow mouth
pitchseat = one short stool | a seat beside the shutter
wickshear = my snipping shears | a little pair of wick nippers
honeyfold = a waxed cake leaf | the honey wrapping
grimegrain = a soot grain | a small oily speck
sealine = the clean edge below the black | a narrow line of light
shutnote = the verse under my breath | a closed-mouth measure

any
opinion @1 strangers against 2 : A caller can ask about the goods. My purse and my tunes aren't on the same stall.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : I'd like the price of a licence to include a place where the roof doesn't empty itself between my collar and my pelt.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : My own patch of Sump will leave a tired voice alone. I wouldn't sell that courtesy cheaply.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Bread available without a fine introduction gives one hungry door a quiet evening. Quiet is a fairly costly thing in the Sump.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : One set of loud boots can turn a dozen conversations into shut mouths. I'd like a better use for leather.
opinion @1 church for 1 : The chapel gets food into a pot and lets a quiet wolf sit by it. I value both pieces of work.

grown
line @1 greet : There's enough light to recognise a caller. Welcome.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : I hear you. Ordinary dealings first.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Still a bit of night caught in my cloth. Welcome.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Keep within the patch that shows your face.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : One lamp needs my full reach. I'll hear you over here.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Draw your stool up to this end.
line @1 again.open : Same face, freshly lit. I remember.
line @1 greet.return : A greeting heard through the last quiet bar.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I know that voice in company or out.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Your words reached past the nippers.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : You have my answer from the lighter patch.
line @1 farewell : Keep one light ahead of your footsteps.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll do the closing verse alone.
line @1 react.news : I'd like a clearer patch on that account.
line @1 react.news.new : That one's arrived without a mark I recognise.
line @1 react.news.known : I've rubbed this piece over once already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Who was in good light when it happened?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Quiet at the hurt door first. An errand after.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Worth opening up a little more light for that.
line @1 answer.how : I've a clean rag end left. Enough to go on with.
line @1 ask.how : Much crowding round your business today?
line @1 sympathise : Hurts worse when every ear turns to hear about it.
line @1 reassure : We can speak through the gap when the crowd goes by.
line @1 decline : I'd keep my private verse clear of all those mouths.
line @1 accept_decline : Closed glass. I can recognise it.
line @1 thank : You've given a quiet task some room.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Leave a lamp in good order for the next tired face.
line @1 preclose : That little dark crescent wants wiping now.
line @1 accept_preclose : I've a rag full of my own business.
line @1 ack : Clear patch.
scene mask
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The ear-shaped smudge is my last bit to wipe off any glass.
b : Couldn't you clean it all together? | Why an ear?
a : Certainly. I just like an audience for my last bit of song before I wipe it off. | That's where the smoke's caught on a curve. I haven't asked the lamp to grow me a nose.

scene cloth
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a different verse into each fold of my cloth.
b : Can a cloth remember words? | Must you fold it exactly right?
a : I do the remembering. Another fold, another chance to put the price of oil out of mind. | It helps. On a busy afternoon the song has been known to start over in the middle.

scene chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save a good quiet chapel for a verse I don't sing in the street.
b : Is the verse especially holy? | Would you sing louder inside?
a : No. It's just dear to me and I'd like its last word clear without a cart going through it. | Smaller voice, actually. A quiet room lets me take it down where I like it.

scene warmhoney
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lamp cloth and a cake wrapper stay in different pockets on my coat.
b : To spare the cloth? | Would you really notice a little soot?
a : For the sake of whoever has to look through honey streaks on a window. The cake has an interest in the matter too. | Yes. I've paid for a honey cake. I want my last mouthful sweet.

scene summertune
when topic=weather self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer leaves enough light for my entire evening verse while there's still a little sky to look at.
b : Is that when you sing for company? | Do you save the last verse for dusk?
a : Company I choose. A window full of strangers would send the words back into my pocket. | I don't save. I keep going till the light or my voice decides for me.

scene buzz
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fly on a sticky lamp rag can make a mind up to be elsewhere quite loudly.
b : Do you help it loose? | Why have you anything sticky there?
a : With a straw. I have no use for a noisy prisoner in my pocket. | The rim of an old lamp can be greasy. Once is plenty for a fly.

scene crowd
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose where my elbows will go before I take a parcel into a crowd.
b : Do you mind a little jostle? | Is there a safe corner to choose?
a : Not for myself so much as the glass. You can only break a lamp once and it'll still be your wages gone. | Near a wall with room to pass. A dead end can fill to the back before you notice.

scene coins
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a market pitch with room for one stool, and an empty corner for the song to go into.
b : Wouldn't you want two stools? | What will you sell?
a : Two make an invitation. One's for my legs after a long morning. Company can come by choice. | Something dry and clean and wanted. First comes the dull part of putting the money together.

scene lampheight
when topic=land self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A low Sump light can do more than a grand high one in the wrong spot.
b : What makes the spot right? | Wouldn't the light go farther up high?
a : If you see a dangerous step before landing on it, that's plenty of height. | Perhaps. A wolf stepping in an unseen hole might have a strong opinion about distance.

scene freshwork
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I try a new task quietly before asking anybody how it should be done.
b : Why not ask first? | Suppose the trick defeats you?
a : I can ask about the actual rough bit instead of standing there saying I'm at a loss. | Then I have a plain question, and enough practice at it to recognise a real answer.

scene stayprivate
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A face seen in lamp glass stays in the lamp glass so far as I'm concerned.
b : Even if it's somebody familiar? | Isn't a reflection public?
a : Especially then. A quiet sighting is no invitation to give an account of another wolf's night. | The light's public. My tongue belongs to me.

scene smalloffer
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My stall coppers go into a pot too slender for idle fingers.
b : Is that safe enough? | How will you get it out again?
a : Safe from my own paw on a hungry morning. For the rest I'll use my own judgement. | Tip the pot over a cloth. Anybody can take one coin. It takes a settled intention to tip them all out.

scene nearfly
when topic=day here.time=dusk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk I test a glass against the bit of sky between two roofs.
b : Aren't you testing whether it shines? | What can you see against the sky?
a : I'm testing what the shine has to get through. I can get that sky for nothing. A second wick costs money. | Every smudge the lamplight would turn gold and let me fancy was clean.

scene familiarfriend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A song I meant for #self.friend# would be a quiet song.
b : How would it reach? | Does the tune get smaller too?
a : I'd wait till there was only the width of a table between us. No point scattering it over the square. | No. A whole tune can sit very comfortably inside a small sound.

scene funded
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If a clean cloth costs a copper I cut it to get two edges of use out of it.
b : Would you sell one edge? | Does the second half stay cleaner?
a : I'd rather save a later copper by having two useful bits of rag. A stall needs both coppers and rags. | If I keep it folded inward. That's the clean edge for a job a customer can see.

scene smells
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can remember a verse from the scent that went with its first singing.
b : Does everything smell of oil after a while? | What smell helps most?
a : Everything in the same pocket does. I keep the very old tunes further away from it. | Plain dry wood after water has gone off the surface. It brings a whole evening back.

scene longroad
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mark out a walk by how often I'll be able to leave the middle of the stream of feet.
b : Do you always need to stop? | Does a quiet lane draw you in?
a : No. It pleases me to know I can choose my pace and still have the glass home in one piece. | If I can see that it's got a way out, yes. I'd like a little choice at the far end, too.

scene shortpray
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sit quietly till the hour suggests a prayer or a song.
b : What distinguishes the two? | What if the silence is enough?
a : Sometimes I don't. The words find the voice that's fit for them. | Then I'll count the quiet as a gift and get up when I'm ready.

story clearear [topic=work self.job=laborer]
  : A lamp had a smoky place that looked so much like an ear I sang part of my song towards it.
  : The glass made no comment. When I finally wiped the patch off the rag carried a perfect black impression.
  b : Did that make a better listener?
  : A travelling one. It rode in my pocket till washing day.

story stoolcoin [topic=dreams]
  : I once tried sitting precisely where I'd put a stool if my own stall appeared overnight.
  : That part of the ground fell away sharply towards a drain. My shoulders went one way and my knees the other.
  b : Would a shorter leg fix the stool?
  : A better patch of ground would save both the leg and the trouble. That's one decision made before buying wood.

story stickyfly [topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes]
  : I wrapped a good honey cake and tied it close round three sides.
  : An ambitious fly went looking at the fourth side just as I folded it shut.
  b : Did supper gain a fly?
  : No. The noise gave away the passenger. I opened a corner and sent the only uninvited guest out again.

rule @working
when concept=bark self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Last wipe across the moving shadow. | Hold the lamp by the cold side.

rule @crowd
when concept=bark self.dislikes=crowds
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Room round the glass, please. | A clear step costs less than a broken lamp.

rule @honey
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Fold the cake clear of the wick cloth. | Don't lay the sweet side down there.

rule @dark
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the glass facing the low step. | Keep the dark rag out of the flame.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I can lend an ear while the glass cools.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : That isn't lamp smoke; it's your face again, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep your paws within the lit bit and I'll hear you.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Light on the step, quiet on both sides. Speak.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=laborer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I leave enough light for a wolf to make the last step in comfort.
dlg @2 resident.job : I'm good for an unhurried paw where a careless one costs glass.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This piece came through unsmudged. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : May the low steps show clear going home.
graft @ear_glass resident.hub
choice Are you really singing to that smudge? -> ear_glass
node ear_glass
say Only till I reach it with the rag. The black curve looks like an ear from this side, and there's no danger it'll take my song out and sell it in the market.
choice What happens when the glass is quite clean? -> ear_glass_more
choice Give the glass its last wipe. -> hub
node ear_glass_more
say I take the last bit of tune home to finish. A good listener doesn't have to be left standing dirty just to keep me company.
choice Give the glass its last wipe. -> hub
choice Step back from the lamp. -> bye
